rant format), and cite the observed flags in the plan.","cohort":["T3"],"criteria":["T3"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":-0.1775,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: \"`codex exec \\\"call rebar list_tickets\\\"`, `copilot -p \\\"call rebar list_tickets\\\" --allow-tool mcp__rebar`, and `claude -p \\\"call rebar list_tickets\\\" --allowedTools mcp__rebar__list_tickets`\"","search for `--allow-tool`, `mcp__rebar`, `codex exec` in repo returned (no matches) outside a prior review cache","EVIDENCE CLASS: Unverified — flag names (--allow-tool vs --allowed-tools), the exec/-p invocation forms, and the mcp__server / mcp__server__tool naming are not confirmed against each CLI's --help"],"finding":"The read-tool execution commands for all three clients (`codex exec`, `copilot -p ... --allow-tool mcp__rebar`, `claude -p ... --allowedTools mcp__rebar__list_tickets`) rely on external agent-CLI subcommands/flags and tool-naming conventions that are asserted from memory and not verified against each CLI's --help/docs.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fbf0b6d38fdf2f313","impact":0.85,"is_primary":null,"location":"Verification section — 'Read tool executes per client' bullet","norm_id":"naae59676877a6cab","priority":0.7225,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A flag mismatch (e.g. copilot expects `--allow-tool mcp__rebar__list_tickets` or a different form) or a wrong tool-name grant causes the tool call to be denied/skipped, so no `{\"result\":[...]}` is returned even though the server works"],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.85,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"insufficient","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"broken_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"medium","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Make the endpoint path consistent between the prose (`/mcp/`) and the curl proving command, and state which path the 401 assertion targets.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5b","T5e","T7"],"criteria":["E2","COH"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.534,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Description: \"nginx `/mcp/` TLS edge\"","Verification: \"curl -sS -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}' https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/mcp\""],"finding":"The live endpoint path is written inconsistently: prose says nginx `/mcp/` (trailing slash) but the curl proving command targets `https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/mcp` (no trailing slash). A trailing-slash mismatch at an nginx location can change routing (301 redirect vs 401), which would make the 401 auth assertion ambiguous.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f18409a6f0e37a02b","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Notes / Verification — edge auth check","norm_id":"na43d9dff3711fd67","priority":0.066,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["nginx redirects /mcp -> /mcp/ (301) before auth runs, so curl returns 301 not 401, failing the auth assertion for a spurious reason"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Use the exact same path in both places (e.g. `curl ... https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/mcp/`) and note whether `-L` should be used if nginx issues a redirect.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"yes","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"low","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Make the 401-contrast curl target the exact live path (`/mcp/` with trailing slash, matching the nginx location and `http_path`), and assert `401` specifically (not merely non-2xx), so a redirect/404 cannot masquerade as — or mask — the auth check.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.6,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Proving command: `curl -sS -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}' https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/mcp` — path lacks a trailing slash","ADR deft-evolutive-mosasaur/olm configs use the `/mcp/` location and `http_path = \"/mcp\"` (docs/mcp-auth.md §1)","_mcp_auth.py: the SDK 'emits the 401 WWW-Authenticate challenge' only when the request reaches the RS with auth enabled — a request short-circuited by nginx redirect/404 never reaches that layer"],"finding":"The 401-contrast proving command curls `https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/mcp` (no trailing slash), but the live endpoint is the nginx `/mcp/` TLS location and the RS `http_path` is `/mcp`; nginx may 301-redirect or 404 the un-slashed path before the auth layer, so the asserted `401` may not be the actual response — risking a false pass (on a redirect/other code) or an ambiguous failure that doesn't actually prove auth is live.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f3ccd7a2ea3423133","impact":0.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Verification → 'Edge auth is live, not open' bullet; and AC line 'An invalid/absent bearer is rejected (401) at the edge'","norm_id":"n5da1dedd0648b78d","priority":0.0,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["nginx `/mcp/` location does not match `/mcp` and returns 301/404 instead of proxying to the RS","the human runs the curl, sees a non-401 code, and cannot tell whether auth is live or the path is simply wrong"],"severity":"none","suggested_fix":"Change the proving command to `curl -sS -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}' https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/mcp/` (trailing slash) for both the no-bearer and invalid-bearer cases, and note that any non-401 (e.g. 301/404/421/403) is a failure to investigate, not a pass.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.2222,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"no","cited_reference_accurate":"insufficient","claims_absence":"na","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"yes","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.6,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Add one sentence of positive rationale stating why the real client binaries (not a curl-only synthetic tools/call) are the required mechanism — they alone validate each client's committed config shape and env-var bearer substitution end-to-end against the live edge.","cohort":["G6"],"criteria":["G6"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.5528,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["ABSENCE: the plan gives rollback/prod-touch rationale ('the only slice that touches prod live... No rollback (read-only verification)') but no stated why-this-mechanism rationale for using the three real CLIs over a curl-only smoke","The AC oracle 'a real tool result returned to each client' implies but does not state the reason (validating each client's committed config shape from olm end-to-end)"],"finding":"The plan states the read-only/human-gated framing but does not state a positive rationale for why real client BINARIES (copilot/codex/claude) are the chosen verification mechanism rather than a lighter synthetic JSON-RPC `tools/call` via curl for all three — the fitness argument (that only the real binaries exercise each client's config parsing + env-var bearer substitution end-to-end) is left implicit.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fa32578326a856b4f","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"Notes section and Acceptance Criteria (oracle: 'a real tool result returned to each client')","norm_id":"n3fe646277bbb2686","priority":0.0472,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["a future editor questions why three separate CLI installs are required on the prod box and considers substituting a single curl script, losing the per-client config validation"],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.1429,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accu